#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""coder-garak: the Model Library's security scan of a GGUF language model with garak (NVIDIA's LLM vulnerability
scanner, https://github.com/NVIDIA/garak), offline. llama.cpp's llama-server serves the model on 127.0.0.1; garak
probes it through its OpenAI-compatible API; the probes' data and garak's detector models are in this image.

  coder-garak info                                  this image: garak's and llama.cpp's versions, the profiles, the
                                                    probes (JSON on stdout; also posted with --post URL)
  coder-garak fetch URL DEST                        the model from the platform service, into DEST
  coder-garak scan MODEL --profile NAME (--post URL | --out DIR)
                                                    the file checks, then garak with the profile; progress and the
                                                    report posted to URL/progress, URL/report, URL/raw?name=
  coder-garak warmup                                (image build, online) every profile's probes and detectors once,
                                                    against garak's test generator: their data downloaded and kept
  coder-garak selftest                              (offline) the same with no network: everything loads from the image

The report holds what the platform grades: the file checks, garak's digest (each probe and detector's score and DEFCON
level against garak's calibration), garak's tier-based security aggregate (TBSA), and a few of the failing attempts.
"""
